# PHASE 2 — CREATE A REUSABLE ANIMATION LIBRARY

I want a reusable animation system with named variants.

The system must allow each section and individual component to select a specific animation instead of forcing all elements through one generic reveal component.

Study and plan the following animation library.

## A. Entrance and reveal animations

1. Split Text Reveal
   - Reveal headings line by line or word by word.
   - Use clipping masks and controlled vertical movement.
   - Suitable for major headings and hero typography.

2. Mask Reveal
   - Reveal artwork through rectangular, diagonal or directional masks.
   - Suitable for game covers, hero artwork and illustrations.

3. Clip-path Wipe
   - Use a moving clip boundary to uncover an element.
   - Suitable for large visual compositions.

4. Blur-to-Sharp
   - Start with a restrained blur and transition into sharp focus.
   - Use sparingly for important visual elements.

5. Scale Depth
   - Use controlled scaling to create a sense of visual depth.
   - Suitable for hero artwork and section transitions.

6. Directional Slide
   - Enter from a selected direction.
   - Use different directions intentionally rather than repeating slide-up.

## B. Cinematic and spatial animations

7. Layered Parallax
   - Move background, artwork and foreground elements at different speeds.
   - Primarily for the hero and selected storytelling sections.

8. Floating Elements
   - Give independent floating movement to interface cards and decorative objects.
   - Use different speeds and directions.

9. Radial Expansion
   - Expand circles, rings and geometric shapes from a central point.
   - Suitable for Bauhaus compositions.

10. Shape Morphing
    - Transform circles, squares, lines and other geometric shapes.
    - Use for problem-to-solution storytelling.

11. Mosaic Reveal
    - Reveal images or visual compositions through individual tiles.
    - Suitable for community and bento-grid sections.

12. Perspective Tilt
    - Add subtle 3D perspective movement to cards on desktop hover.
    - Disable or simplify pointer-dependent movement on mobile.

## C. Storytelling and interaction animations

13. Draw-on Animation
    - Progressively draw SVG lines and paths.
    - Suitable for workflows, timelines and connected diagrams.

14. Horizontal Cascade
    - Alternate elements entering from the left and right.
    - Suitable for feature collections.

15. Podium Rise
    - Raise first, second and third-place podiums independently.
    - Suitable for the leaderboard.

16. Accordion Expansion
    - Animate FAQ content opening and closing.
    - Animate the corresponding indicator icon.

17. Line Draw
    - Draw connecting lines progressively as the section enters view.

18. Image Zoom
    - Slowly zoom artwork inside a clipped image container.
    - Suitable for game and tournament cards.

19. Number Transition
    - Animate numeric values only when they are real data.
    - Never invent statistics or animate fabricated values.

20. Magnetic Microinteraction
    - Add restrained pointer response to eligible desktop buttons and controls.
    - Preserve usability and accessibility.

### Animation specification requirements

For each animation, document:

